  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "id": "azure-hub-spoke-reference",
    "title": "Azure hub-and-spoke reference architecture",
    "environment": "reference",
    "assumptions": [
      "Synthetic reference architecture for authoring and rendering checks. Nothing here describes deployed Azure infrastructure.",
      "Region: the brief names none, so Southeast Asia (southeastasia) is assumed. No availability zones are declared, so the VM and node pool zones stay unspecified.",
      "Tenant, subscription and all entity names are placeholders. Address spaces, SKUs, tiers, VM size and OS are not declared.",
      "Resource groups: one for the hub and one for the spoke, as briefed. Azure Monitor is placed in the hub resource group; the brief did not say where.",
      "Ownership (scope_refs) and network attachment are declared separately. A resource group is never inferred from the VNet or subnet an entity attaches to.",
      "The overview shows network and location only; the subscription and resource groups appear only in the ownership view, so ownership is not implied by nesting.",
      "Subnets: the hub has AzureFirewallSubnet and GatewaySubnet; the spoke has a workload subnet (VM and NIC) and an AKS node subnet. The brief did not list subnets.",
      "Peering is one undirected relationship between the hub and spoke VNets. Gateway transit, forwarded traffic and user-defined routes are not declared.",
      "Azure Firewall and VPN Gateway sit in the hub with no traffic links, and no on-premises endpoint is modelled, because the brief supplies none.",
      "The NSG is associated with the NIC; the brief did not say NIC or subnet level, so no subnet association is declared.",
      "VM-to-SQL (TCP 1433) and VM-to-Blob (HTTPS) are the only data-path flows, taken from the spoke application intent. The network path (private endpoint, firewall) is not declared.",
      "Microsoft Entra ID (tenant-scoped, global) and Azure Monitor have no relationships because the brief supplies none; they are shown as context.",
      "AKS: the cluster and node pool attach to the spoke VNet and AKS node subnet, in the same subscription and spoke resource group. The managed control plane is not drawn.",
      "Kubernetes names, the two-replica Deployment and the Pod-to-Node placement are declared by the author for the reference, not observed from a live cluster.",
      "The Deployment, not each Pod, references the PVC, Secret and ServiceAccount, as a workload template would. The NetworkPolicy is drawn against the Deployment; its rules are not declared.",
      "The Ingress controller is cluster-level with no namespace, and its implementation is not named. No load balancer or other entry point in front of it is declared.",
      "Storage: the PVC is bound to a PV with a StorageClass. No Azure disk or file share backing the PV is modelled. The Secret is a reference only and holds no value."
    ],
    "description": "Reference scenario T-002: one subscription with separate hub and spoke resource groups and VNets, explicit peering, a spoke VM and managed services, plus an AKS companion in the same subscription and spoke VNet. Synthetic; not deployed infrastructure."
  },
